rInvocations to clear. Do you actually need to reset the listener? The following check is true, not checking false again."],["c8f9d854_8b090daf",135,0,1,"Please change it back, and update the one in line 92 as suggested by Wenyu."]],0,308],[7169741,20412,56,1.341,1.058,[[56,0.902,3,52],[57,0.098,2,4]],[["d37e9755_93bcd8cf",136,-1,1,"Don't forget to add the string to this CL."]],0,309],[7180074,20413,9,0.592,0.327,[[15,11]],[["339db595_f88190bd",137,0,0,"Since you override setEnabled(), I would assume you also need to override isEnabled() to check mSwitch etc, no?"]],0,310],[7199185,20416,30,0.737,0.556,[[10,0.757,34,24],[17,0.243,66,6]],[["eb9abb90_76ff11d2",138,0,1,"nit: Rename this variable for consistency"]],0,311],[7200426,20416,122,2.361,1.866,[[10,35]],[],0,312],[7199709,20416,5,0.259,0.185,[[56,4]],[],0,313],[7200292,20417,3,0.143,0.09,[[10,36]],[],0,314],[7205388,20418,21,0.796,0.587,[[17,67]],[],0,315],[7208361,20419,13,0.384,0.302,[[13,22]],[],0,316],[7203960,20419,339,7.601,6.192,[[56,5]],[["0d089592_559933b7",139,-2,1,"This shouldn't in a binder() function."],["2cd8f27d_2129d562",139,-2,1,"This looks wrong, it should be moved to ALL_NTP_CARDS_SWITCH_ON_CHECKED_CHANGE_LISTENER."],["4241085d_b62b58df",140,-2,0,"Please add a single property key for this."],["9c854eca_7dca8de5",139,-2,1,"This class no longer exists, please update."],["c5aa4cb3_cf0259b6",128,-2,1,"I feel this test is for coordinator, while the rest should moved to NtpCardsBottomSheetViewBinderUnitTest. This could make writing tests easier."],["7278e793_14ba3ea6",141,-1,0,"Add @VisibleForTesting annotation if needed only for tests."],["739c6650_3c21ab5f",142,-1,1,"Move the bind() to setup using the PropertyModelChangeProcessor.create() function."],["8c9eafde_44dd8752",139,-1,1,"Super nit: add a blank line below."],["bcd3d407_718e987f",139,-1,1,"Is there any case the else is true?"]],0,317],[7201184,20425,609,10.971,8.929,[[10,0.571,37,346],[17,0.409,68,253],[16,0.013,66,7],[5,0.008,5,3]],[["12b67d6c_2fbd1173",143,-2,1,"This looks really similar to the original version. Is it identical? Can we share code somehow?"],["1fe1e041_79a3fcfe",143,-2,0,"Why does this thing's constructor take a `@Nullable Drawable image` and then proceeds to assert it's not null? This doesn't make sense to me."],["35931589_049446ea",144,-2,1,"This is really confusing how you're mutating the visibility of the animation view from multiple properties, that are going to have to be set in a sequence, that's not immediately obvious."],["3d7ffdd4_ff471d39",143,-2,1,"Why is this a Promise? What does this conceptually represent? I'm having a hard time understanding."],["5ea4ac40_02e04814",145,-2,1,"Why is the coordinator involved with the mediator and the view working together to begin with? I don't understand why this code is here."],["7ba46334_b0d06701",144,-2,1,"This is really clunky. Why do we need this? IMO this is backwards, the coordinator should manage the children, not the other way around."],["b3d1d411_f68b3bcf",138,-2,1,"Is this a race and we just do the wrong thing if things don't sequence correctly? This worries me. Maybe we should wait for native to init somewhere."],["ba4d8fe9_e42d60a1",143,-1,0,"Nit: You're exposing a class here that arguably should be view side only. But you do need to know if it was successful or not. You could have like a Callback<Boolean>, but your approach is probably…"],["f7cf11c1_2ba4a816",143,-1,1,"Can you add a comment explaining the purpose of this? This is after the animation finishes, right?"]],0,318],[7224765,20425,8,0.421,0.3,[[10,38]],[],0,319],[7224533,20431,192,3.856,3.092,[[58,0]],[["1558dcb8_4983cf90",146,-5,1,"Should this be `static jlong`?"],["4dcb8921_d4583226",147,-4,1,"Just stopping by here in this CL because I spend a good day trying to figure out why this was succeeding to build locally but failing in the CQ: we recently introduce the need to add a DEFINE_JNI…"],["7d60db63_aad642f3",147,-4,1,"We need a `DEFINE_JNI()` at the bottom now: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7232750"],["ca25b89e_73648e9c",148,-4,1,"I believe this is the issue causing JNI to fail. The java target needs to be depended upon by another java target, not a C++ target."],["3bac9f82_43572497",147,0,1,"Do we need conversions for int -> jint and bool -> jboolean? Or is it not needed?"],["7e35d4db_d8bddf82",149,0,1,"Nit: please `#include <string>`"]],0,320],[7247464,20433,60,1.379,1.017,[[5,0.364,6,36],[59,0.196,0,18],[10,0.084,39,6],[60,0.084,0,6],[17,0.065,69,6],[61,0.065,0,6],[62,0.056,0,4],[63,0.056,0,4],[7,0.028,173,2]],[["86da0a6f_6acb0677",150,0,1,"nit: The original drawable comes with a different tint. Is this change ok? If we are unsure, let's just update the `follow_add` drawable, (and add some comments) to match the ic_add_24dp to limit the…"]],0,321],[7237400,20434,191,4.21,3.407,[[48,0.854,2,167],[58,0.085,1,15],[11,0.025,15,4],[47,0.025,6,4],[21,0.01,21,1]],[["4b2cf7b8_ed857d76",151,-3,1,"So now that we are anchored to a profile, I think we need to handle Profile's potentially going away - unless there's a reason we can assume they outlast us? If not, then wire up a ProfileObserver:…"],["b8cf539d_304261fd",152,-3,0,"Is there a more specific type we can use here?"],["136dd6a9_26e1b4f4",153,-2,1,"Do you need some equivalent for the java? Maybe that's why the headers are missing? Maybe the java needs a dep to get access to the JNI headers?"],["22f7f040_5fe12562",153,-2,1,"If you replace this with a regular dep like \":jni_headers_java\", would that fix things?"],["3ecbd559_335b5bb2",153,-2,1,"Also wrote in another comment, does this need a dependency on the jni headers maybe?"],["b244e413_c713e826",153,-2,1,"Did we need a jni_zero dependency somewhere here?"],["93bd2022_e209458e",124,0,1,"I think you'll want to assert this is non-zero. Otherwise you're passing it down into native without any checks and a reinterpet_cast. This could end up in use-after-free at that point."]],0,322],[7256856,20435,86,2.113,1.57,[[16,0.921,67,80],[6,0.079,37,6]],[["36792738_5625233e",133,-1,1,"Similar comment as above, but it seems like we're checking for the incognito window string here, even though the `emptyTitleInstance` has `isIncognitoSelected = false`"],["3ee2f037_75675b2b",4,-1,1,"Can we only ever hit this for incognito windows? Or should we also account for non-Incognito empty windows? There's also this helper [1] (that accounts for custom titles, emptiness, incognito, etc.),…"],["86773ad9_6e662971",154,-1,1,"Was this intended to be added to this CL? I think this verifies the same thing as when there's only one tab in the group [1]. Is that expected to change? [1]…"],["99cafabd_2fea84e7",4,-1,1,"nit: Use local variable to help indentation"]],0,323],[7265779,20438,51,1.144,0.818,[[16,0.911,68,48],[6,0.054,38,2],[7,0.036,174,1]],[["656543ae_8de70066",19,0,1,"No access, but the CL lgtm"]],0,324],[7256749,20441,11,0.403,0.275,[[7,175]],[["45758a1c_1e245d68",155,-1,0,"So, will `url` forever be non-`null`? I see it is currently, but is that a guarantee?"],["83ff89e4_239174e9",155,-1,1,"Are we planning on ever reading the new parameter?"],["b0eb6b39_1134984d",155,-1,1,"Home page URLs may already contain query strings. We should use GURL in this function and GURL modification libraries to add a query param"],["6c58e9c2_d023dbc5",156,0,1,"I don't think you need this anymore."]],0,325],[7278295,20445,61,1.22,0.938,[[47,7]],[],0,326],[7362349,20453,2,0.13,0.082,[[64,0]],[],0,327]]}